WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.092 --> 00:00:01.412
- We're here with Eugene Levy,

00:00:01.412 --> 00:00:05.094
give it up!

00:00:05.094 --> 00:00:06.502
His new book is called

00:00:06.502 --> 00:00:08.810
Best Wishes Warmest Regards,

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:09.930
the story of Schitt's Creek.

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:11.590
It's out right now.

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:12.770
I miss Schitt's Creek.

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:13.603
Do you miss it?

00:00:13.603 --> 00:00:14.990
Cause it was such a great cast.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:15.823
- I actually do.

00:00:15.823 --> 00:00:16.952
I do miss it.

00:00:16.952 --> 00:00:19.600
I miss doing it.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.310
When we actually wrapped the series,

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:22.893
I said to myself,

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:25.200
what are we doing?

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.940
This is so going on.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:30.090
But, it was the right decision.

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:30.923
- Yeah, ugh.

00:00:30.923 --> 00:00:32.110
I mean maybe.

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:32.943
It was such a-

00:00:32.943 --> 00:00:33.780
I was so sad.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:34.650
- Well, you never want

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:35.540
to take a chance

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:37.260
that you're going to
go into another season,

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.983
then it's just not going
to be quite as good.

00:00:40.983 --> 00:00:42.310
- I get it, I get it,

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:44.245
but at the same time, mad, whatever.

00:00:44.245 --> 00:00:46.070
And do you ever watch old episodes,

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:47.330
like when they come on?

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:51.200
- Well, now that the show
is in syndication of,

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.033
you know,

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:53.330
when you're kind of channel flipping,

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:57.320
I will sometimes see the show on the air,

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:59.580
and to be honest,

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.940
I can watch it now

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:05.307
as if I wasn't really in it.

00:01:05.307 --> 00:01:06.140
You know?

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:07.690
I mean I can actually watch it

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:09.830
as a television episode,

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:12.210
just to see how everything holds up,

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:13.170
you know,

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.120
because when you're doing a show,

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.680
you have a tendency sometimes

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:19.930
to maybe only look at yourself

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:22.020
when you're looking at the show.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:23.030
I don't know if you ever

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:25.230
kind of go through that at all,

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:26.860
but you find yourself focused

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:28.640
on yourself quite a bit,

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:30.010
just to see how am I doing?

00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:30.843
How am I, you know,

00:01:30.843 --> 00:01:31.820
how do I look in this scene?

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:32.653
Well that's great.

00:01:32.653 --> 00:01:33.590
I mean, this is great.

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:35.850
I'm holding up my end of the scene.

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:38.460
And then the more you kind of,

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:39.293
you know,

00:01:39.293 --> 00:01:41.810
see it during the editing process

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:42.643
and everything else,

00:01:42.643 --> 00:01:44.320
the more you're looking at an episode,

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:46.930
then you kind of notice
everything else, right?

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:49.560
But it's an actors thing I think.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.440
I don't honestly know if

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:53.460
it's possible for an actor to look

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.350
at himself in a scene

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:57.930
and look at the scene
without looking at himself.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:58.763
I mean, it's-

00:01:58.763 --> 00:01:59.596
- I was gonna say that's yeah.

00:01:59.596 --> 00:02:00.810
Well, it is amazing though,

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:01.730
to point out though,

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:03.190
editors are amazing

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:04.730
because after doing the voice,

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:07.280
like it's one of those
things where you're in it.

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:08.420
So you, like you said, you're in it,

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:09.580
you're doing your thing,

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:10.580
but then you watch it back

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:11.760
and how they edit it together.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.600
These people are so
gifted at what they do.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.280
They make you look funnier.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.113
They make you like,

00:02:17.113 --> 00:02:17.946
they make the show better.

00:02:17.946 --> 00:02:18.779
I'm just like, wait,

00:02:18.779 --> 00:02:19.930
that's not how it happened.

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:20.763
What? that was like,

00:02:20.763 --> 00:02:22.020
Yeah, they make us look way better.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.220
The editors are amazing.
- Yeah, cause there's

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:24.980
too many moments you can remember

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:26.670
as being kind of bad moments

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:28.510
that I wish I could take back,

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:29.920
and yet you don't see it.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:30.946
- They're good.

00:02:30.946 --> 00:02:32.140
- When it's in in the
final product, Right?

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:34.410
Because they've, they have snipped it out.

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:35.243
- Yeah.

00:02:35.243 --> 00:02:36.076
- Good.

00:02:36.076 --> 00:02:36.909
- I know, God bless them.

00:02:36.909 --> 00:02:38.960
So why did you like really?

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.640
Why did you want to
write a book on the show?

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.990
- You know, our fans are,

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:45.776
when it comes to Schitt's Creek knowledge,

00:02:45.776 --> 00:02:49.060
they are the most intelligent,

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:50.000
they're like Mensa.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.000
They they know every single thing

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:53.833
about the show,

00:02:53.833 --> 00:02:56.770
so we wanted to give them a book

00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:58.997
that they would find interesting,

00:02:58.997 --> 00:03:00.660
and things in the book

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:02.490
that they actually would find interesting,

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:06.910
and not necessarily know everything about.

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:07.743
Right?

00:03:07.743 --> 00:03:11.100
And on social media over the years,

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.723
when we were doing our show,

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:15.770
a lot of great stuff would come out

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:16.650
in social media,

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:19.710
the, you know, people would be painting

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:21.000
you know, things,

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.210
and caricatures,

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:24.830
and settings and scenes.

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:28.510
And we used a lot of that fan art

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:30.756
in the, in the book

00:03:30.756 --> 00:03:33.020
as an acknowledgement

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:34.870
to the people who actually went above

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:37.050
and beyond in helping

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:39.550
to promote the show that they loved.

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:40.910
And it's the actors talking

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:42.590
about their characters,

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:45.060
and talking about their favorite scenes

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:46.563
in the show and,

00:03:47.849 --> 00:03:48.682
oh God,

00:03:48.682 --> 00:03:49.515
everything you wanted

00:03:49.515 --> 00:03:51.490
to know about Moira's wigs.

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:54.700
And it's, I mean, it's all in there,

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.070
and we're hoping

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.687
that the fans really, really love it.

00:03:59.687 --> 00:04:00.740
- Oh, I imagine there'll be so proud too.

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:01.930
It's so cool of you to involve them.

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:02.763
Like, you know,

00:04:02.763 --> 00:04:03.760
to have them be a part of it as well.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:04.593
That's so cool.

00:04:04.593 --> 00:04:05.730
- Well, they were such a big part

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.930
of the success of our show

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:09.540
because they, you know,

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:11.150
social media,

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.810
when people take to what you do

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:14.650
and they're so passionate about it.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:15.580
- It can turn things around.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:17.008
- It can really turn things around.

00:04:17.008 --> 00:04:19.160
They can't stop talking about it

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:20.480
and it became infectious.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:23.110
It really helps spread the word.

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:25.470
So this was like a little love letter

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:27.860
to our fans.

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:29.920
- Well, speaking of
wigs, you brought it up.

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:31.793
The book has this picture of you,

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:34.523
which is fantastic.

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:36.540
So what's going on here

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:38.363
and how many drugs were you on?

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:42.525
- Well, that was a take-

00:04:42.525 --> 00:04:44.480
(Eugene laughing)

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:46.440
that was taken on our,

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:49.090
after we wrapped the series,

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:50.620
after our very last scene,

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:51.480
doing the show,

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:56.080
which was outside of the Rosebud motel.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:59.350
And we finished,

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:01.570
we popped some champagne

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:07.683
and I was feeling rather Merry.

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:11.640
And one of Moira's wigs

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:14.850
was being kind of passed around one

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:16.960
of the trailers at that point.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:18.160
And we were all kind of,

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:18.993
you know,

00:05:18.993 --> 00:05:20.660
in there together telling stories,

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:22.650
and congratulating each other,

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:25.110
and crying and saying goodbye.

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:27.500
And somebody put the wig on me,

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:31.441
and I, it felt so good.

00:05:31.441 --> 00:05:32.940
(Laughter)

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:33.930
- I do feel like you should have

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:34.810
an English accent

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:36.470
and you should be stoned.

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:38.910
I think it would be a
really great character

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:39.910
for something.

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:41.550
Well, Dan, read some things

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:43.780
on the show just to tease you, right?

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:44.800
What was one?

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:47.330
I heard it had to do something
maybe with your hair.

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:50.616
- Yeah, well, yeah, there was one,

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:51.449
(Laughter)

00:05:51.449 --> 00:05:52.890
- I love this episode

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:53.723
- that's the one.

00:05:53.723 --> 00:05:54.670
Okay, I'm a little picky

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:57.650
about my hair and it's not,

00:05:57.650 --> 00:06:01.530
you know, it's not vanity it's not vanity.

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:03.850
It's just really tough hair

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:06.640
to do, you know, for me.

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:10.260
I mean, I'm looking at
it now and it's like,

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:12.610
it's got a little whoopity doo curl

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:13.443
in the front.

00:06:13.443 --> 00:06:15.350
I can't do anything about it.

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:17.890
So I'm kinda touchy about,

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:19.530
you know, just getting my hair,

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:20.930
It takes a while to get my hair

00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:23.280
to look the way I think it should.

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:25.170
He wrote an episode called the drip,

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:26.380
where I'm lying in bed

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:28.610
and all night a drip has been dripping

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:32.580
on my head and I wake up soaked.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:34.960
And I, you know, when I read the scene,

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:35.793
I said,

00:06:35.793 --> 00:06:36.963
ah, Dan really?

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:39.610
It can't drip anywhere else,

00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:41.290
except on my hair?

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:42.123
I mean, yeah,

00:06:42.123 --> 00:06:44.199
okay, okay, I'll do it.

00:06:44.199 --> 00:06:46.153
We were shooting the scene,

00:06:47.270 --> 00:06:48.160
and I take a break

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:49.670
and I look in that little hand mirror.

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:51.240
I said, can I borrow a little mirror

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:53.110
and I check the mirror

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:54.930
and I'm going, okay.

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:56.920
It's all right.

00:06:56.920 --> 00:06:58.570
I think I can live with this.

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:00.360
And then I hear a voice saying,

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:02.223
I think it should be more wet.

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:04.763
That was Daniel

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:06.863
It was Daniel.

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:09.700
And I said, really?

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:10.533
He said, yeah,

00:07:10.533 --> 00:07:11.366
I don't think it's going to play

00:07:11.366 --> 00:07:14.193
Unless it, it's really
got to look like it's wet.

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:17.800
- This is for not getting
him something at Christmas.

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:19.820
- Yeah this is, it's from something.

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:20.830
And I could never

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:23.920
to this day track exactly what it was,

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:25.580
but we did the scene

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:28.770
and he got such a kick out of it.

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:29.910
Honestly, I mean,

00:07:29.910 --> 00:07:32.410
I got as much fun watching him,

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:35.050
watching me being as miserable

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:36.753
as I was doing the scene,

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:39.400
but it all worked for the scene,

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:40.233
and I got it,

00:07:40.233 --> 00:07:42.070
and I knew why the hair had to be wet.

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:43.300
So I went ahead and did it.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:44.565
- You leaned in.

00:07:44.565 --> 00:07:45.398
- I leaned in.

00:07:45.398 --> 00:07:47.437
- That's a real man y'all.
- Well I'm a pro.

